name w3-07-mig-cap-1
timeout 520
time 1991-01-19T00:00:00Z

# CAMPAIGN W3, SORTIE 7 OF 10 - THE DEFENDING CAP, FLOWN THE WAY THE TYPE WAS DESIGNED TO BE FLOWN.
# Spec, anchor and sources: doc/campaigns/w3-desert-storm.md. Format: doc/missions/campaign.md.
# CONTROL: none - it IS the control, of w3-08-mig-alone.fbm.
#
# THE ANCHOR: about 55 Iraqi fighters were aloft in the Package Q area on 19 January (25 MiG-23,
# 20 MiG-25, 10 MiG-29) [T4]; across the opening days six Iraqi MiG-29s were shot down by F-15Cs and
# NONE scored an air-to-air kill, and the explanation the sources give is not the aeroplane: poor
# training, NO AEW SUPPORT, and flying "essentially alone, without the tactical architecture the design
# assumed" [T4]. This file and w3-08 are that sentence turned into an experiment.
#
# THE ONE DELETED LINE, AND THE POLICY IT IS MEASURED UNDER (rule 11, and it is the reason this pair is
# in the campaign at all). `o1-02`, `o1-03`, `o5-03` and `o2-04` already ran "the same deleted line"
# (`set brief_gci`) in four theatres and DISAGREED. O2 found why: the deciding line is not the brief but
# `set n019_emission`. O1 and O5 spawned their MiGs `illum`, so deleting the brief left the antenna
# badly AIMED; O2 spawned them in the documented power-up state `off`, where the brief's THIRD typed
# entry is the only thing in the tree that ever turns the radar on. W3 IS THE FIFTH THEATRE AND IT
# DECLARES ITS POLICY IN ADVANCE: `set n019_emission off`, O2's. The comparable quantity is therefore
# "what the controller is worth GIVEN a silent power-up state", and the campaign predicts O2's answer
# rather than O1's. ATTRIBUTION RUN A3 is w3-08 with that one token changed to `illum`, so this campaign
# measures the policy instead of assuming it.
#
# THE SUBSTITUTION AND ITS DIRECTION: the MiG-29 stands in for the MiG-23/MiG-25 that were ~45 of the 55
# [T4]. FlightBox's MiG-29 has a look-down N019, an IRST and the SPO-15; a MiG-23ML has a 23 km look-down
# set and a MiG-25PD a +4.5 g limit (doc/modules/air/catalogue.md). RED IS THEREFORE MATERIALLY STRONGER
# THAN HISTORY, and a FlightBox result that still goes badly for Red says something STRONGER than the
# record did, while one that goes well says nothing about 1991. The catalogue rows for those two types
# EXIST and are deliberately NOT used: both are `ALPHA` (doc/modules/air/module.md, A10), and an ALPHA
# row may not answer a campaign question.
#
# THE ARENA is w3-03's, with the target set moved to 44.36-44.52 E and the CAP holding east of it; every
# coordinate is [SET]. `--elev const`, 0 m datum, no terrain masking (C4).
# WHICH DEFENSIVE LAYER THIS FILE MEASURES: the FIGHTER layer. The surface layer is present and briefed
# to hold - a P-18 that radiates from t = 0 and a ZSU-23-4 that cannot reach a 5 000 m ingress at all -
# and it fires nothing. O5's rule that two layers cannot be measured in one file holds here too.
# NIGHT: 03:00 local, sun about -48 deg [DERIVED]. Nothing in this tree emits light, so BOTH MERGES IN
# THIS PAIR ARE EYELESS: `sensors/FBVisualSystem` contributes nothing after dark, and every detection in
# both files is a radar or an infrared one. That is a limit on the CLAIM, not on the mechanism.
#
# THE TWO ENGAGEMENTS ARE SEPARATED IN TIME (O1's rule): the strikers release at t = 172 / 188 s at
# 44.36-44.40 E; the fighter merge runs from t = 194 s onward, 100 km further east and 6 s later. A run
# ends at the FIRST flight-monitor K.O. and a mission-killed fighter takes ~50-120 s to reach the ground,
# so the strike had to be complete before the first kill or it would not be in the record at all.
#
# THE ONE TACTICAL QUESTION: AGAINST AN OPPONENT FLOWN THE WAY THE TYPE WAS DESIGNED TO BE FLOWN -
# ground-vectored, radar silent until the controller's third call - does the F-16's earlier detection
# still convert into an earlier shot?
#
# MEASURED (fingerprint 38a02bbbe00b3e99):
#   Red's first look   `radar RADAR_CONTACT unit=q7mig1 track=1 rangeNm=52.76` at t = 54.9 s. 50 Red
#                      contact lines over the run
#   Red's shots        five launch solutions - `q7mig2` R-27R t = 195.4 at 15.05 km, `q7mig3` t = 204.8
#                      at 13.38 km, `q7mig4` t = 205.8 at 13.51 km, then two R-73 at t = 210.1 / 219.5
#   Red's arrivals     ONE, `q7mig2_r27r_3` on `q7escb` at 12.94 m against a 13.8 m fuze - INSIDE the
#                      fuze and NOT a kill, which is O2's rule 13 arriving in a sixth theatre
#   Blue               first solution t = 196.5, i.e. 1.1 s AFTER Red's; one AIM-120 at 2.47 m kills
#                      `q7mig1` at t = 211.3
#   the strike         2 of 2 released at t = 174.6 / 190.0, both aim points destroyed, 21 s and 5 s
#                      before Red's first shot - the time separation held
#   the run            ends t = 272.8 on `q7mig1`'s ground contact, 61.5 s after its combat kill
# SO THE ANSWER TO THIS FILE'S QUESTION IS NO, AND SHARPLY: with the controller present the F-16's
# detection advantage does NOT convert into an earlier shot. Red shoots first, by 1.1 s. What Blue has
# instead is the round: 2.47 m and a kill against 12.94 m and none.
#
# WHAT TO READ:
#   events.log      the FIRST `radar RADAR_CONTACT unit=q7mig*` (the quantity this pair compares),
#                   `sms LAUNCH_SOLUTION` per side with its range, `stores DETONATION` with `missM`
#                   against the round's own `fuzeM`
#   telemetry_q7mig1.csv  n019_emission and the antenna commands - the brief's three typed entries
#
# READING RULE: exit 3 = TIMEOUT is expected; this file is a measuring rig. THE MEASUREMENT IS THE
# TRIPLE (first Red radar contact, Red shots, Red arrivals) read beside w3-08-mig-alone.fbm, which is
# this file with one line deleted. Read the DETECTION TIMES, not the kills: O2 measured two R-27R inside
# their own fuze that did not kill and one further out that did, so an outcome axis ordered by kills is
# reading warhead arrival geometry.

net kari7
  control q7nod
  link wire
  period 4.0
  hold 3
  wcs free
  member q7nod
  member q7flk autonomy hold

unit q7stra
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight st7 1
  spawn 33.20000 43.85000 5000 90.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 80
  set fcr_mode off
  set attack_mode ccrp
  set rwr on
  set datalink on
  set store 3 mk84
  set store 7 mk84
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  wp 33.20000 44.36000 5000 450
  wp 33.20000 43.90000 5000 450
  objective kill unit q7tgt
  objective survive

